Z||000011||Mach10||08-25-2001||03:50 PM||||That's odd. All that from a flaming nightie? I wouldn't think that the burns from that would be life-threatening. I was under the impression that anything over 1/3 of the body being 3rd degree was life-threatening. <BR>I'm surprised that she died within a few hours. How sad. <P>There must have been something else. 100g of nylon/poly burning shouldn't be enough to burn 1/3 of skin surface area to 3rd degree burns. I saw one where a hair-spray can exploded in some guys hands, and set his clothes on fire. That wasn't pretty. 2nd, 3rd degree burns to 2/3 of his body. Took him forever to heal up. Skin grafting is marvellous technology, though.||||reg||5
